OL,3,GNEWSADetective kept child abuse case
OL,4,Aevidence at home
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former detective has been banned from
OL,7,Fpolicing after mobile phones linked to
OL,8,Fchild abuse investigations were found
OL,9,Fin his house.
OL,11,FDet Con James Cox, formerly of West
OL,12,FMidlands Police, kept a large amount of
OL,13,Fevidence at home, including 11 phones,
OL,14,FUSB devices, briefing packs and his
OL,15,Fairwaves police radio.
OL,17,FIt came to light in January last year,
OL,18,Fwhen his supervisor asked about the
OL,19,Fwhereabouts of a phone containing
OL,20,Fevidence in a child abuse case.
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
